@startuml kernel-structure
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 70
skinparam ranksep 60

title Dependency direction — the kernel never sees a feature

rectangle "**starling**  «binary»\ncomposition root\nthe only crate that names both sides" as bin #FFF8DC

rectangle "**starling-state**\nServerCore · Dispatcher\nEventBus · Capability impls" as kernel #E6F0FA

rectangle "**feature crates**\npchat · audit · calendar\nfile-server · wasm-host" as feats #EAF7EA

rectangle "**starling-api**  «traits only, no logic»\nStateQuery · Feature\nEventSubscriber · Capabilities" as api #F5E6F5

bin --> kernel
bin --> feats

kernel --> api : depends on
feats  --> api : depends on

kernel -[#Red,dashed]-> feats : **never** — CI asserts this

note bottom of api
  Both sides depend on the traits.
  Neither depends on the other.
  ""cargo tree"" fails the build on any
  ""starling-state"" -> ""starling-feature-*"" edge.
end note

@enduml
